to run a program

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:20.730
to try to reduce
their churn rates.

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:22.822
So what they did is
they took a look at,

00:12:22.822 --> 00:12:24.530
within all of their
data, their analytics

00:12:24.530 --> 00:12:27.213
data from their website
and their apps, what kind

00:12:27.213 --> 00:12:28.880
of signals could
predict a customer that

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:30.800
was likely to churn.

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:32.840
And what they found
was a couple factors

00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:35.660
were pretty good predictors
of a customer likely to churn.

00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:39.230
Things like a customer turning
off automatic bill pay,

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:42.780
or a customer who stops
engaging with their mobile app.

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:45.110
So what they did is
inside of Analytics 360,

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:47.840
they created an
audience for just users

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:50.252
who met that exact criteria.

00:12:50.252 --> 00:12:52.460
Then they shift that audience
over to Display &amp; Video

00:12:52.460 --> 00:12:56.000
360, where they ran an
ad program targeted just

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:58.670
to those users to try to
remind them of the value

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:02.480
that Sprint offers and keep
them within their network.

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:04.330
And the results, you
